Fixed simulation profile settlement

The qualified native-wait capability is orthogonal to one known PPU/APU
profile. Common selection intersects occupied-seat capabilities once, prefers
the common native APU variant, then enables wait ownership only if common.
Unknown selections, multiple PPU/APU profiles and legacy-plus-wait are refused.
The sealed bootstrap identity binds the canonical session and selected profile.
Executable/content SHA checks remain independent and mandatory.
